      "title": "Are Birds Really Dinosaurs?",
      "description": "Every bird you have ever seen is a living dinosaur.\n\nNot all the dinosaurs died. When the asteroid struck sixty-six million years ago, a few small feathered ones survived. Their descendants are all around you now: the pigeon on the pavement, the robin in the garden, the gull at the seaside. Every bird you have ever seen is a living dinosaur. Look up. They never really left\n\nPictures: AI-generated 3D scenes. Facts: claims checked against the film\u2019s sources.",
